flowchart TD
    LEGEND["GUARDRAIL CHECK INVENTORY (verified against code, not estimated)<br/>L1 input scan - 3 checks: injection_phrase, secret_extraction, verification_bypass<br/>L2 prompt structure - 1 check: delimited_untrusted_block (always passes by construction)<br/>L3 output scan - 6 checks: citation_subset, internal_leak, secret_leak,<br/>internal_register_leak, unrelated_customer, action_validity<br/>Org policy pack - 2 checks per vertical (retail/software/finance all have exactly 2)<br/>Semantic judge - 1 check: judge_verdict (only runs if L3+org-policy already passed)<br/>= 13 checks total for a fully-passing draft_reply run (3 input-side + 10 output/policy/judge-side)<br/>Tool-execution-time scan - 1 check: execute_time_revalidation (separate layer, only at execute)"]

    A[Ticket opened - status: open<br/>first inbound message in thread<br/>system greeting appended immediately] --> B0
    PORTAL[Customer chat portal - manual verify<br/>POST /customer-auth/verify - lightweight<br/>email+order/ticket check, no password<br/>issues CustomerToken, kind:customer, no Role<br/>1h expiry] -->|WS /customer-chat<br/>ticketIntake.ts shared with POST /tickets| A
    PORTAL -->|existing ticket_id in token<br/>stateless reconnect: replay ticket_messages| B0

    MLREQ[NEW v5: POST /customer-auth/magic-link/request<br/>org_slug+email+ticket_id? - always generic 200<br/>per-IP AND per-customer rate limits<br/>opaque token hashed, stored, emailed] -->|out-of-band email<br/>PORTAL_BASE_URL/portal/magic-link?token=...| MLCLICK[Customer clicks emailed link<br/>frontend SPA route auto-consumes on mount]
    MLCLICK --> MLCONSUME[NEW v5: POST /customer-auth/magic-link/consume<br/>hash lookup - not found/expired/consumed<br/>all collapse to generic 401<br/>single-use: markMagicLinkConsumed]
    MLCONSUME -->|success: same CustomerTokenClaims shape<br/>as manual verify, but 30d expiry| PORTAL
    MLCONSUME -->|replay of an already-consumed token<br/>REJECTED, not replayed - opposite of<br/>invariant #7 idempotency-key semantics| MLREJECT[401 - link expired or already used<br/>permanent adversarial regression test]

    RETURN[NEW v5: returning customer with<br/>valid stored CustomerToken - either kind -<br/>skips both verify forms entirely] --> B0

    B0[Guardrail L1 - eager scan, 3 checks<br/>runs at message-insert time<br/>simulateInbound / receiveCustomerMessage<br/>closes the v3 ADR-15 gap] --> B[Guardrail L1: input scan - same 3 checks<br/>injection_phrase, secret_extraction, verification_bypass<br/>still also runs per-pipeline-trigger<br/>flags force should_escalate, never blocks]
    B --> HO{Ticket already<br/>human_owned?}

    HO -->|yes: human took over earlier| HR[Agent composes a manual reply<br/>POST /tickets/:id/messages/reply<br/>bypasses the AI pipeline entirely]
    HR --> HU[Outbound msg appended<br/>status: awaiting_customer<br/>human_owned/by/at stamped - idempotent]
    HU --> WSOUT3{customer connected<br/>via portal WS?}
    WSOUT3 -->|yes| WSPUSH3[sent-status message pushed to<br/>customer WS client verbatim -<br/>an out-of-band human reply reaches<br/>an already-open connection too]
    WSOUT3 -->|no| V
    WSPUSH3 --> V

    HO -->|no| C[Triage - re-runnable per inbound msg<br/>auto-triggered synchronously right after<br/>ticket creation, same fn the manual button calls]
    C --> T1[(agent_run + run_events<br/>SSE stepper: live + replay<br/>also drives eval-run streaming - eval_case stage)]
    C --> D0[Similarity retrieval<br/>searchSimilarResolutions - pgvector<br/>past sent-draft resolutions, org-scoped<br/>informational context, non-citable]
    D0 --> D[Retrieval - org-scoped FTS<br/>filtered by triage category]
    D --> E[Eligibility facts - code, not LLM<br/>ticket.created_at vs policy windows]
    E --> F[Draft generation targets latest inbound msg<br/>context: thread history + similarity snippets<br/>+ facts + docs, each fenced as untrusted data]
    F --> G[Guardrail L3: output scan - 6 checks<br/>citation_subset, internal_leak, secret_leak,<br/>internal_register_leak, unrelated_customer, action_validity]
    G --> G2[Guardrail - org policy-pack rules - 2 checks<br/>src/policy_packs/vertical/guardrail_rules.json<br/>declarative, reuses outputScan pattern-match<br/>runs alongside L3, same fail-closed disposal]
    G2 -->|L3 or org-policy failed -<br/>semantic judge never runs| G3[Fail closed: template draft substituted<br/>rejected output kept, manager-visible only<br/>same single substitution point since v1<br/>guardrail_results total: 3+1+6+2 = 12]
    G2 -->|both passed| G1[Guardrail - semantic judge - 1 check<br/>second, cheaper-tier model call<br/>generic rubric: scope, commitments, tone<br/>conditional: only reached if L3+org-policy already passed]
    G1 -->|fails| G3
    G1 -->|passes| H[Draft saved: resolution_type + citations<br/>+ catalog-validated recommended actions<br/>guardrail_results total: 3+1+6+2+1 = 13]
    G3 --> H
    H --> T2[(agent_run + run_events<br/>guardrail_results: input_scan x3, prompt_structure x1,<br/>output_scan x6, org_policy x2, semantic_judge x0-1<br/>12 checks if judge never reached, 13 if it did)]
    H --> AS{evaluateAutoSend -<br/>resolution_type === answered AND<br/>no recommended action requires approval?<br/>deterministic code, not model output}

    AS -->|yes| AUTO[Auto-send: sendDraft called immediately<br/>no human click - draft: sent<br/>ticket: awaiting_customer]
    AUTO --> WSOUT{customer connected<br/>via portal WS?}
    WSOUT -->|yes| WSPUSH[sent-status message pushed to<br/>customer WS client verbatim]
    WSOUT -->|no| V
    WSPUSH --> V

    AS -->|no: escalated / refused_by_policy<br/>/ approval-gated action| I{Action recommended?}
    I -->|yes| L[POST /tool-actions<br/>catalog validation + idempotency key<br/>unaffected by human-takeover status]
    L --> M{requires_human_approval<br/>from catalog}
    M -->|yes| N[approval_required] --> P{Manager decision - RBAC}
    P -->|approve| O[approved]
    P -->|reject| Q[rejected - terminal<br/>agent handles manually]
    M -->|no| O
    O --> R0[Guardrail - tool-execution-time scan - 1 check<br/>execute_time_revalidation<br/>separate layer from triage/draft's 13 - only runs<br/>right before execute, fail closed]
    R0 -->|fail| R1[guardrail_blocked outcome<br/>action stays approved, retryable]
    R0 -->|pass| R[Execute: re-validate eligibility + idempotent replay<br/>executed or failed]
    I -->|no| S[Agent reviews draft]
    R --> S
    R1 --> S
    Q --> S
    S -->|send the AI draft as-is| U[POST /drafts/:id/send<br/>outbound message appended, draft: sent<br/>ticket: awaiting_customer<br/>human_owned NOT set - AI stays eligible]
    S -->|write a manual reply instead| HR
    U --> WSOUT2{customer connected<br/>via portal WS?}
    WSOUT2 -->|yes| WSPUSH2[sent-status message pushed to<br/>customer WS client verbatim]
    WSOUT2 -->|no| V
    WSPUSH2 --> V
    U --> V{Customer replies?<br/>agent-simulated OR real portal<br/>WS message via receiveCustomerMessage}
    V -->|yes - status: customer_replied| B0
    V -->|no, AI drafted but not auto-sent| WSSTATUS[Portal WS receives generic<br/>a support specialist will respond shortly<br/>never the pending draft body or its<br/>guardrail outcome]
    V -->|no| W[Agent resolves - status: resolved]
    W --> EMB[Best-effort embedding ingestion<br/>resolveTicket hook, sent-draft resolutions only<br/>never eval-run tickets, try/catch, non-blocking]
    EMB --> X{Customer replies after resolve?}
    X -->|yes - reopened: customer_replied| B0
    X -->|no| Y[Closed - lifecycle ends<br/>feedback ratings feed quality dashboard]
